## 🔧 Troubleshooting

**❌ Plugin doesn't load at all.** Check `scte_module` path in `uplynk.conf`
matches where you copied the file. Check file permissions (`644` or looser).
Check the slicer log for Python import errors.

**😶 Plugin loads but doesn't react.** Check `channel_group` in `uplynk.conf`
matches one of this build's presets: {% for m in methods %}`{{ m.channel_group }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. A typo here means the dispatcher's fallback fires (no-op with a warning log).

**⚠️ "channel_group X not recognized" in the log.** Same as above — dispatcher
didn't match `channel_group` to any registered method.

**📭 SCTE-35 messages arrive but nothing fires.** Bump `scte_log_verbosity` to
`3` and re-check. Verify the message's segmentation type_id is one this
preset handles (see [🎬 Presets](#-presets-included-in-this-build) above).

**⏰ Ad breaks fire at the wrong time.** For `live_event`, tune `pts_offset_*`
and `duration_offset_*` in `uplynk.conf`. Small float values (fractions of
a second) are normal.

**🔣 UPID decoding shows binary hex instead of a readable string.** Not a bug
— the UPID isn't UTF-8 text (probably a binary EIDR or MPU identifier).
The hex is the raw payload; decode it upstream if you need a semantic value.

