# 📚 SCTE-35 refresher

📖 SCTE-35 is the SMPTE standard for carrying ad-insertion and program-boundary
cues in an MPEG transport stream. Each message contains a **command** and
zero or more **segmentation descriptors**.

## 🎮 Command types

| 🔢 Value | 🏷️ Name | 🎯 Meaning |
|----------|---------|------------|
| `0x00` | `splice_null` | 💓 Heartbeat, no action |
| `0x04` | `splice_schedule` | 📅 Scheduled splice (rare in live) |
| `0x05` | `splice_insert` | 📢 The classic ad-break signal (in/out points, duration) |
| `0x06` | `time_signal` | 🕒 Timing marker; usually paired with a segmentation_descriptor |
| `0x07` | `bandwidth_reservation` | 📊 Reserved capacity signal |
| `0xFF` | `private_command` | 🔒 Vendor-specific extension |

💡 Most modern SCTE-35 in the wild is either `splice_insert` (command_type 5)
or `time_signal` with a segmentation descriptor (command_type 6).

## 🔢 Segmentation type_ids (the ones you'll see most)

| 🔣 Hex | 🔢 Dec | 🏷️ Name |
|--------|--------|---------|
| `0x00` | 0 | ⚪ Not Indicated |
| `0x10` | 16 | 🟢 Program Start |
| `0x11` | 17 | 🔴 Program End |
| `0x13` | 19 | ⏸️ Program Breakaway |
| `0x14` | 20 | ▶️ Program Resumption |
| `0x20` | 32 | 📖 Chapter Start |
| `0x21` | 33 | 📕 Chapter End |
| `0x22` | 34 | 🎬 Break Start |
| `0x23` | 35 | 🎞️ Break End |
| `0x30` | 48 | 📣 Provider Advertisement Start |
| `0x31` | 49 | 🔚 Provider Advertisement End |
| `0x34` | 52 | 🎯 Provider Placement Opportunity Start |
| `0x35` | 53 | 🏁 Provider Placement Opportunity End |
| `0x36` | 54 | 📡 Distributor Placement Opportunity Start |
| `0x37` | 55 | 📴 Distributor Placement Opportunity End |
| `0x40` | 64 | ⚡ Unscheduled Event Start |
| `0x41` | 65 | 🛑 Unscheduled Event End |
| `0x50` | 80 | 🌐 Network Start |
| `0x51` | 81 | 🔌 Network End |

🔗 Start/end type_ids come in pairs (34/35, 48/49, 54/55, etc.) — a `Start`
means "an event is beginning at this PTS", the matching `End` means
"it's over". Some workflows use `Provider` types (0x30/0x31) for ads
inserted by the network; others use `Distributor` types (0x36/0x37) for
ads inserted by the affiliate.

## 🆔 UPIDs

🔖 Every segmentation descriptor can carry a **UPID** (Unique Program
Identifier) — a variable-length payload identifying what's being signaled.
UPID types include ad-ID, EIDR, ISAN, TID, MPU, and free-text formats.

🛡️ The `scte_logger` preset (if included in this build) tries UTF-8 decoding
first and falls back to raw hex if that fails — because binary UPIDs are
common in the wild.

